---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { operatorContact } from '../../../../scripts/site-config.mjs';
import { contactMailto } from '../lib/contact';
const contact = operatorContact(process.env);
---
<SiteLayout title="Contact & error reports" description="How to report a calculation error, a page problem or a question about this project collection, and which details help reproduce an issue." noindex={!contact.complete}>
  <section class="border-b border-line bg-[#eff5f3] py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact & error reports</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Help make the next result clearer.</h1>
      <p class="body-copy mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg">Questions about this collection, an unexpected Tile Planner result, or a page that does not work as expected belong here. A few precise details make an issue easier to check.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="shell">
    <section aria-labelledby="contact-heading" class="grid gap-6 py-12 sm:grid-cols-[0.7fr_1.3fr] sm:gap-12">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The contact channel</p><h2 id="contact-heading" class="section-title mt-3">Get in touch.</h2><p class="body-copy mt-4">For website questions and corrections. The tools cannot certify an installation or replace advice for your specific materials and site.</p></div>
      {contact.email ? <div class="panel min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Email the operator</h3>
        <p id="contact-email" class="mt-4 select-all text-lg font-semibold text-teal [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">{contact.email}</p>
        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
          <a class="button" href={contactMailto(contact.email)}>Write an email</a>
          <button type="button" id="copy-email" data-email={contact.email} class="min-h-12 rounded-lg border border-teal px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-teal hover:bg-[#eff5f3]" aria-describedby="copy-status">Copy email address</button>
        </div>
        <p id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="body-copy mt-4 text-sm">You can also select and copy the address above.</p>
        <p class="body-copy mt-3 text-sm">Write an email opens your configured mail app with a report outline. Review it and send from that app. This page does not send messages or confirm delivery. If no mail app opens, paste the address into your usual email service.</p>
      </div> : <aside class="panel" aria-labelledby="email-notice">
        <h3 id="email-notice" class="text-lg font-bold">Local preview · contact email pending</h3>
        <p class="body-copy mt-3">The operator has not yet supplied a public contact email. There is currently no working contact channel on this page, and no report can be submitted here.</p>
        <p class="body-copy mt-3 text-sm">You can prepare the details below, but they will not be delivered through this site. This incomplete contact page is marked not to be indexed until an address is provided.</p>
      </aside>}
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="report-heading" class="border-t border-line py-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">A useful error report</p><h2 id="report-heading" class="section-title mt-3">Show how to reach the same result.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4 max-w-3xl">For a calculation or layout issue, include the exact values as displayed. For a general question, the page and a short description are enough.</p>
      <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        <li class="panel"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold">1. The page and steps</h3><p class="body-copy mt-3">Name the project and copy the page or article URL. Describe the steps from opening the page to seeing the problem, including any unit switch, reset or link you followed.</p></li>
        <li class="panel"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold">2. Exact inputs and units</h3><p class="body-copy mt-3">List room width and length, tile width and length, and the unit for each. Include allowance %, tiles per box and optional USD price per box. For layout, add grout in mm, rotation and corner or center start.</p></li>
        <li class="panel"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold">3. Observed and expected results</h3><p class="body-copy mt-3">Quote the result or error message you saw and what you expected instead. Explain your comparison or calculation. A cropped screenshot can help show a display problem; include the values as text too.</p></li>
        <li class="panel"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold">4. Browser and device</h3><p class="body-copy mt-3">Include the browser name and version, phone or computer, and operating system if known. Say whether the issue repeats after reloading and whether it affects a specific screen size.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <aside class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-[#eff5f3] p-6 sm:p-9" aria-labelledby="privacy-note">
      <h2 id="privacy-note" class="section-title">Share the issue, not private details.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4 max-w-3xl">Remove names, home addresses, account details and unrelated browser tabs from screenshots. Never send passwords, payment information or access tokens. Review copied URLs: tool links can contain room measurements and other inputs. Include only the details you are comfortable sharing that are needed to reproduce the issue.</p>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4 max-w-3xl">Before reporting a count difference, check whether you are comparing purchased tiles with placed full tiles and cut pieces. The layout does not optimize cutting or reuse. <a class="text-link" href="/projects/tile-planner/#walkthrough">Compare the worked example</a> or read the <a class="text-link" href="/about/#corrections">correction principles</a>.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
<script>
  import { copyContactEmail } from '../lib/contact';
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-email');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#copy-status');
  if (button && status) button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const email = button.dataset.email;
    if (!email) return;
    button.disabled = true;
    status.textContent = 'Copying email address…';
    status.textContent = await copyContactEmail(email, navigator.clipboard);
    button.disabled = false;
  });
</script>
